Open Agentic Engineering Framework (OAEF)
Copyright 2026 Felipe Carvalho. All rights reserved.

Created and authored by Felipe Carvalho.

This framework establishes a vendor-neutral, mathematically bounded open standard
for software engineering workflows operated by autonomous AI coding agents
and human engineers.

Foundational Influences and Citations:
- Andrej Karpathy: The LLM Wiki architecture, continuous structured synthesis,
  and documentation maintenance scripts.
- Google: Open Knowledge Format (OKF) semantic YAML frontmatter metadata.
- Jeremy Howard & Answer.ai: The /llms.txt standard for machine-readable discovery.
- Very Good Ventures (VGV): Clean Code philosophy, strict static analysis, and
  rigorous 100% automated test coverage culture.
- Michael Nygard: Architecture Decision Records (ADR) for immutable historical records.
- Dan North & Martin Fowler: Behavior-Driven Development (BDD) and executable specifications.
- Robert C. Martin (Uncle Bob): Clean Code craftsmanship, meaningful names,
  single responsibility, clean sizing limits, and ban on abbreviations and flag arguments.
- Cyrille Martraire: Living Documentation concepts and executable architectural contracts.

Original OAEF Innovations by Felipe Carvalho:
- The Inviolable Trust Hierarchy (Compiler > Tests > Source Code > Docs > Memory > Hallucination).
- The 4 Pillars of Agentic Software Engineering.
- Zero-Docker / Zero-Daemon Living Memory (Session Handoff & Append-Only Ledger).
- Stack-Adaptive Agent Skills Catalog.
- Multi-Tool IDE Synchronization Engine (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, .cursorrules, .windsurfrules).
- Algorithmic Multidimensional Quality Gates with the Monotonic Ratchet Rule.
- The Architectural Discovery Interview Protocol.

